 in super determinism  you know everything is already  determined there is no quantum  randomness  inequality violations can be explained  by  super determinism  and  yeah at least she's very consistent that  uh certainly grant her  but when  when she claims that science has proved  it for instance  that free will is an illusion  she goes too far  and she goes too far by taking  mathematics too uh  literally can you quickly outline to the  audience what super determinism is  perhaps what you dislike about it  yeah well actually there are two things  that i dislike so firstly is already  determinism let me come back to that but  so you know the entire future like the  entire past everything is already  determined doesn't mean that we know it  or it doesn't even mean that we have any  ability to  get that knowledge  but you know  ontologically fundamentally it is  already determined that's determinism  now when people say  super determinism  they add an extra little assumption  namely that  um  okay it's that everything is coordinated  because you could still imagine that you  know this part of the universe is  entirely determined  that part is also entirely determined  but they are not yet connected so we are  still independent systems that exist in  the world  now if you i if you also reject the  existence of in  independent systems  then this is  super determinism some other people  would probably  say that super the super of super  determinism means  a kind of conspiracy because when these  these different things not only needs to  be already  connected so not  independent but they have to be not  independent in a very specific way for  instance to explain the violation or the  apparent violation of bell inequality so  i certainly dislike completely the idea  that there exists no independent systems  in the universe  and actually my my view is  very clearly i mean physics has to be  able to tell stories physics should make  predictions we all know that and  predic